# TypeScript

`tsconfig.base.json` enables `strict`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, `verbatimModuleSyntax`, `noUnused*`. Never weaken these per-package or per-file.

- No `any`. Use `unknown` and narrow (`instanceof`, `in`, Zod `parse`). If truly unavoidable, add an `eslint-disable-next-line` with a reason.
- No `@ts-ignore`; `@ts-expect-error` only with an explanatory comment.
- No non-null assertions (`!`) to silence errors — handle the `undefined` case.
- Type-only imports use `import type` or inline `type` (required by `verbatimModuleSyntax`).
- Derive types instead of duplicating them: `z.infer<typeof schema>`, `typeof X[keyof typeof X]`, `Pick`/`Omit` on shared DTOs.
- Prefer `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions/compositions; `as const` objects over `enum`.
- Explicit return types on exported functions and service/repository methods.
- Avoid `as` casts except at trusted boundaries (e.g. parsed JSON already validated).

```ts
// ❌
function load(id: any) { return cache[id]!; }

// ✅
function load(id: string): Project | undefined {
  return cache[id];
}
```
